<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="{{@site.locale}}">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />

    {{!-- Content Security Policy.

         Defense-in-depth: even if an XSS vector slips past every
         sanitizer, the browser refuses to execute scripts from
         off-allowlist origins, refuses connect-src to off-allowlist
         hosts, and blocks framing of this page.

         Tradeoffs we accept:
         - 'unsafe-inline' on script-src is REMOVED. Every theme-side
           inline <script> has been externalized (assets/js/boot/*,
           assets/js/page/*, assets/js/reader.js, etc.); template-data
           bindings (MO_API_BASE, mo-digest-assets) are emitted as
           <meta> tags read by tiny bootstrap scripts. If Ghost's
           {{ghost_head}} or admin Code Injection injects inline JS,
           those will be blocked — verify Plausible / analytics still
           load (Plausible's proxied build is an external <script>,
           so it should be fine).
         - 'unsafe-inline' on style-src for inline style="..." attrs
           on Ghost-rendered post bodies + a few theme spots.
         - img-src https: is broad; Ghost feature_images come from
           any admin-configured CDN (HubSpot CDN during migration,
           Ghost CDN after).

         frame-ancestors is HTTP-header-only (not supported in meta).
         Set via Ghost Pro's Cloudflare in front, or accept that
         click-jacking surface is unmitigated for now.

         Pass 2 A05-1, A05-2, A05-3. --}}
    {{!-- connect-src is named-host, not wildcard. `https://*.workers.dev`
         would allow any attacker.workers.dev as a JWT exfiltration
         target (Codex audit 2026-05-11: "MOAuth.fetch sends member
         JWTs to any URL"). The 12 hosts below are exactly the workers
         that BACKEND-INVENTORY.md §6 lists as theme-callable. New
         worker → add it here AND to the MOAuth.fetch allowlist
         harvest in admin-auth.js. --}}
    <meta http-equiv="Content-Security-Policy" content="default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://unpkg.com https://cdn.jsdelivr.net https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://js.stripe.com; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src 'self' https://fonts.gstatic.com data:; img-src 'self' data: blob: https:; media-src 'self' https:; frame-src 'self' https://www.youtube.com https://www.youtube-nocookie.com https://player.vimeo.com https://player.captivate.fm https://js.stripe.com https://challenges.cloudflare.com https://embed.spotify.com https://open.spotify.com https://mo-test.ghost.io; connect-src 'self' https://mo-admin.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-audio.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-ebook-access.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-errors.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-forms.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-gift.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-kit.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-kit-bridge.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-membership.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-pdf.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-podcast-feed.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mo-search.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev https://mereorthodoxy.com https://www.mereorthodoxy.com https://mo-test.ghost.io https://api.stripe.com https://plausible.io https://challenges.cloudflare.com; form-action 'self' https://challenges.cloudflare.com; base-uri 'self'; object-src 'none'; upgrade-insecure-requests" />
    <meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin-when-cross-origin" />

    <title>{{meta_title}}</title>
    <script src="{{asset "js/boot/title-fix.js"}}"></script>
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#1d1b18">

    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://js.stripe.com" />
    <link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://plausible.io" />
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IM+Fell+Great+Primer:ital@0;1&family=Source+Serif+Pro:ital,wght@0,400;0,600;0,700;1,400;1,600&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />

    <link rel="stylesheet" type="text/css" href="{{asset "built/screen.css"}}" />

    {{!-- No-JS fallback: screen.css hides "Parent > Child" nav items
         pre-JS to prevent the flicker before nav-dropdowns.js rebuilds
         them into dropdowns. If JS doesn't run at all, this <noscript>
         re-shows them so the children stay reachable. --}}
    <noscript>
        <style>
            [data-nav-dropdowns] a[data-nav-label*=">"] { display: inline-flex; }
        </style>
    </noscript>

    {{!-- Membership API base URL. mo-api-base.js (loaded with the
         other boot scripts) reads this and sets window.MO_API_BASE
         for the membership-related JS to consume. Externalizing the
         per-template inline setter lets us drop 'unsafe-inline' from
         the CSP. --}}
    <meta name="mo-api-base" content="{{@custom.membership_api_base}}" />

    {{#if @custom.content_api_key}}
    <meta name="ghost-content-api-key" content="{{@custom.content_api_key}}" />
    {{/if}}

    {{!-- Trusted destinations for MOAuth.fetch. admin-auth.js reads
         this ONCE at IIFE time (before {{{body}}} renders, before any
         page-template scripts run) and freezes the set. Pipe-separated
         URL list because some values may contain commas or spaces in
         the future; pipe is reliably URL-safe.

         Codex audit 2026-05-11 (P0 finding): the previous
         implementation harvested allowlisted hosts from
         [data-worker-url], [data-kit-bridge-url], [data-api-base]
         elements in the DOM and re-harvested on a miss. An XSS could
         inject <div data-worker-url="https://attacker.example"> and
         then call MOAuth.fetch on attacker.example — the new element
         got harvested on miss, attacker host became trusted, JWT went
         to attacker. Closure-private prevented extraction but
         DOM-injection extended the allowlist.

         Hardcoded here at template render time so the runtime never
         re-reads DOM-mutable state. New worker → add its URL to this
         list AND to the connect-src directive in the CSP above. --}}
    <meta name="mo-trusted-hosts" content="{{@custom.kit_worker_url}}|{{@custom.admin_worker_url}}|{{@custom.search_worker_url}}|{{@custom.error_worker_url}}|{{@custom.podcast_feed_url}}|{{@custom.membership_api_base}}|{{@custom.gift_worker_url}}|{{@custom.kit_bridge_url}}|https://mo-audio.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev|https://mo-pdf.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev|https://mo-forms.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev|https://mo-ebook-access.mo-podcast-feed.workers.dev" />

    {{!-- Cloudflare Turnstile site key. Public-by-design (key is
         visible in the rendered widget anyway). Hardcoded as a meta
         tag rather than a Ghost @custom setting because @custom is
         at the 20-setting cap. site-forms.js reads it on contact +
         submissions pages. Codex audit 2026-05-11 follow-up. --}}
    <meta name="turnstile-site-key" content="0x4AAAAAADNUmqxNMMwe32iy" />

    {{!-- Turnstile JS. Loads on every page so any future form that
         wants bot protection can render <div class="cf-turnstile">
         without per-template script tags. Async + defer so it doesn't
         block first paint. --}}
    <script src="https://challenges.cloudflare.com/turnstile/v0/api.js" async defer></script>

    <script type="application/ld+json">
    {
      "@context": "https://schema.org",
      "@type": "Organization",
      "name": "Mere Orthodoxy",
      "url": "{{@site.url}}",
      "logo": "{{@site.logo}}",
      "description": "{{@site.description}}",
      "foundingDate": "2005",
      "sameAs": [
        "https://x.com/maborodoxy",
        "https://www.facebook.com/mereorthodoxy",
        "https://www.instagram.com/mereorthodoxy"
      ]
    }
    </script>

    <meta property="og:image" content="{{asset "images/mo-share-card.jpg"}}" />
    <meta property="og:image:width" content="1200" />
    <meta property="og:image:height" content="630" />
    <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{asset "images/mo-share-card.jpg"}}" />

    {{ghost_head}}

    {{!-- Plausible tracker is injected by Ghost's official Plausible
         Integration via ghost_head (proxied through the Ghost domain
         as pa-*.js, which bypasses ad blockers). Do NOT add a direct
         <script src="plausible.io/..."> here: plausible.io/js/* is on
         every major blocklist, so the request fails, and Ghost's
         proxied build installs its own window.plausible without
         replaying a queue shim — any event pushed to the shim before
         the real sender loads is silently dropped.

         Custom events (e.g. "Article Read" on posts) fire via
         window.plausible(...) on the 'load' event — after pa-*.js has
         installed the real sender. See post.hbs for the one caller. --}}

    <link rel="icon" type="image/jpeg" href="{{asset "images/mere-o-fav-icon.jpg"}}" />
    <link rel="shortcut icon" type="image/jpeg" href="{{asset "images/mere-o-fav-icon.jpg"}}" />
    <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{asset "images/mere-o-fav-icon.jpg"}}" />
</head>
<body class="{{body_class}}"
      {{#if @custom.podcast_feed_url}}data-podcast-feed-url="{{@custom.podcast_feed_url}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @custom.kit_worker_url}}data-kit-worker-url="{{@custom.kit_worker_url}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @custom.search_worker_url}}data-search-worker-url="{{@custom.search_worker_url}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @custom.admin_worker_url}}data-admin-worker-url="{{@custom.admin_worker_url}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @custom.error_worker_url}}data-error-worker-url="{{@custom.error_worker_url}}"{{/if}}
      {{#if @member}}data-member-email="{{@member.email}}" data-member-status="{{@member.status}}"{{/if}}>

    {{!-- Liturgical calendar: applies the season class to <body> before
         first paint to prevent FOUC. Loaded synchronously (no async/
         defer) so it runs after <body> is parsed but before paint.
         Full settings UI lives in liturgical-calendar.js further
         down the body. --}}
    <script src="{{asset "js/boot/liturgical-class.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/boot/mo-api-base.js"}}"></script>

    {{!-- admin-auth + safe-href MUST load before {{{body}}} below.
         Page templates (custom-dashboard.hbs, custom-bookmarks.hbs,
         etc.) include their own <script> tags inside {{{body}}}, and
         those scripts call window.MOAuth.fetch / window.MOSafeHref.set
         synchronously on load. If admin-auth.js is loaded later in
         default.hbs (after {{{body}}}), the page-template scripts run
         first and throw "Cannot read properties of undefined (reading
         'fetch')" — and because that throw happens before a Promise
         is even constructed, the .catch handlers in dashboard.js
         never fire and modules stay stuck on their "Loading…"
         placeholder. See HANDOFF_3.1 for the full debug chain. --}}
    <script src="{{asset "js/admin-auth.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/lib/safe-href.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/lib/safe-redirect.js"}}"></script>
    {{!-- DOMPurify (vendored, ~22KB). Loaded globally so any script
         that pastes HTML into innerHTML has it available. Was
         previously per-template (custom-events, custom-dashboard-
         replays, custom-forum); Codex audit 2026-05-11 added
         faith-received.js to the list. Loading once here is simpler
         than adding the script tag to all 77 faith-received template
         files. --}}
    <script src="{{asset "js/vendor/purify.min.js"}}"></script>

    <header class="site-header">
        <div class="container header-inner">
            <a href="{{@site.url}}" class="brand" aria-label="{{@site.title}} home">
                <img src="{{asset "images/mere-o-logo.png"}}" alt="{{@site.title}}" class="brand-logo" />
            </a>
            <nav class="nav" aria-label="Primary" data-nav-dropdowns>
                {{!-- Use this.url so Handlebars resolves the nav item's
                     `url` property instead of invoking Ghost's {{url}}
                     helper, which was returning "/" for every item.
                     `data-nav-dropdowns` triggers nav-dropdowns.js to
                     regroup flat items into dropdowns using the
                     "Parent > Child" label convention managed in
                     Ghost Admin → Settings → Navigation. --}}
                {{#foreach @site.navigation}}
                    <a href="{{this.url}}" data-nav-label="{{label}}">{{label}}</a>
                {{/foreach}}
            </nav>
            <div class="nav-actions">
                {{!-- Search trigger — opens Ghost's built-in sodo-search
                     modal (auto-loaded by ghost_head). Keyboard "/" also
                     opens it. --}}
                <button class="nav-search" type="button" data-mo-search aria-label="Search articles">
                    <svg class="nav-search-icon" width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle>
                        <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"></line>
                    </svg>
                </button>
                {{#unless @member}}
                    <button class="sign-in" data-portal="signin">Sign in</button>
                    <a href="/membership/" class="btn btn-primary">Become a Member</a>
                {{else}}
                    <a href="/dashboard/" class="btn btn-primary btn-account">{{#if @member.name}}{{@member.name}}{{else}}Dashboard{{/if}}</a>
                {{/unless}}
            </div>
            <button class="nav-toggle" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="mobile-nav" aria-label="Open menu">
                <span class="nav-toggle-bar"></span>
                <span class="nav-toggle-bar"></span>
                <span class="nav-toggle-bar"></span>
            </button>
        </div>
    </header>

    <div class="mobile-nav" id="mobile-nav" hidden>
        <div class="mobile-nav-backdrop"></div>
        <aside class="mobile-nav-panel" role="dialog" aria-label="Site navigation">
            <div class="mobile-nav-head">
                <span class="mobile-nav-wordmark"><em>{{@site.title}}</em></span>
                <button class="mobile-nav-close" type="button" aria-label="Close menu">&times;</button>
            </div>
            <nav class="mobile-nav-links" aria-label="Primary" data-nav-dropdowns data-nav-mode="mobile">
                {{#foreach @site.navigation}}
                    <a href="{{this.url}}" data-nav-label="{{label}}">{{label}}</a>
                {{/foreach}}
            </nav>
            <div class="mobile-nav-actions">
                <button class="mobile-nav-search" type="button" data-mo-search aria-label="Search articles">
                    <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true">
                        <circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle>
                        <line x1="21" y1="21" x2="16.65" y2="16.65"></line>
                    </svg>
                    <span>Search articles</span>
                </button>
                {{#unless @member}}
                    <button class="mobile-nav-signin" data-portal="signin">Sign in</button>
                    <a href="/membership/" class="btn btn-primary">Become a Member</a>
                {{else}}
                    <a href="/dashboard/" class="btn btn-primary btn-account">{{#if @member.name}}{{@member.name}}{{else}}Dashboard{{/if}}</a>
                {{/unless}}
            </div>
        </aside>
    </div>

    {{{body}}}

    <footer class="site-footer">
        <div class="container site-footer-grid">

            <div class="site-footer-col site-footer-brand">
                <a href="{{@site.url}}" class="site-footer-brand-link" aria-label="{{@site.title}} home">
                    <img src="{{asset "images/mere-o-logo.png"}}" alt="" class="site-footer-logo" />
                    <span class="site-footer-wordmark"><em>{{@site.title}}</em></span>
                </a>
                <p class="site-footer-tagline">Christian renewal for the common good.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="site-footer-col">
                <h4 class="site-footer-heading">Social</h4>
                <ul class="site-footer-list">
                    {{#if @site.twitter}}
                        <li>
                            <a href="https://x.com/{{@site.twitter}}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
                                <svg class="site-footer-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18.244 2H21l-6.51 7.443L22 22h-6.91l-4.41-5.79L5.5 22H2.74l6.95-7.945L2 2h7.06l3.99 5.27L18.244 2zm-2.426 18h1.86L7.27 4H5.3l10.518 16z"/></svg>
                                <span>X</span>
                            </a>
                        </li>
                    {{/if}}
                    {{#if @site.facebook}}
                        <li>
                            <a href="https://facebook.com/{{@site.facebook}}" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
                                <svg class="site-footer-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M22 12.06C22 6.5 17.52 2 12 2S2 6.5 2 12.06c0 5.02 3.66 9.18 8.44 9.94v-7.03H7.9v-2.91h2.54V9.85c0-2.51 1.49-3.9 3.77-3.9 1.09 0 2.24.2 2.24.2v2.46h-1.26c-1.24 0-1.63.78-1.63 1.57v1.88h2.78l-.45 2.91h-2.33V22c4.78-.76 8.44-4.92 8.44-9.94z"/></svg>
                                <span>Facebook</span>
                            </a>
                        </li>
                    {{/if}}
                    <li>
                        <a href="https://www.youtube.com/@MereOrthodoxy" rel="noopener" target="_blank">
                            <svg class="site-footer-icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M23.5 6.2a3 3 0 0 0-2.1-2.1C19.5 3.5 12 3.5 12 3.5s-7.5 0-9.4.6A3 3 0 0 0 .5 6.2C0 8.1 0 12 0 12s0 3.9.5 5.8a3 3 0 0 0 2.1 2.1c1.9.6 9.4.6 9.4.6s7.5 0 9.4-.6a3 3 0 0 0 2.1-2.1c.5-1.9.5-5.8.5-5.8s0-3.9-.5-5.8zM9.6 15.6V8.4l6.2 3.6-6.2 3.6z"/></svg>
                            <span>YouTube</span>
                        </a>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="site-footer-col">
                <h4 class="site-footer-heading">About</h4>
                <ul class="site-footer-list">
                    <li><a href="/about/">About</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/contributors/">Contributors</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/membership/">Support Our Work</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/contact/">Contact</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a></li>
                </ul>
            </div>

            <div class="site-footer-col">
                <h4 class="site-footer-heading">Podcasts</h4>
                <ul class="site-footer-list">
                    <li><a href="/podcasts/mere-fidelity/">Mere Fidelity</a></li>
                    <li><a href="/podcasts/christians-reading-classics/">Christians Reading Classics</a></li>
                </ul>
            </div>

        </div>

        <div class="container site-footer-bottom">
            <p class="site-footer-meta">
                &copy; {{date format="YYYY"}} {{@site.title}}. {{@site.title}} is a publication of the non-profit Institute for Christianity and Common Life. All rights reserved.
            </p>
            {{#if @site.secondary_navigation}}
                <nav class="footer-nav" aria-label="Secondary">
                    {{#foreach @site.secondary_navigation}}
                        <a href="{{this.url}}">{{label}}</a>
                    {{/foreach}}
                </nav>
            {{/if}}
        </div>
    </footer>

    {{!-- jsonld-fix.js corrects Ghost's auto-emitted Article JSON-LD
         to use the real byline (author-* tag) instead of the generic
         "Mere Orthodoxy" house account, and adds SearchAction to the
         homepage WebSite block. Loaded high in the body so the fix
         lands before render-pass crawlers (Googlebot, PerplexityBot,
         Bingbot) snapshot the page for indexing. See file header for
         the full rationale. --}}
    {{!-- Error beacon: posts uncaught JS errors, unhandled promise
         rejections, and CSP violations to the mo-errors worker so
         we see what's actually breaking in production browsers. No-
         op when @custom.error_worker_url is empty. --}}
    <script src="{{asset "js/error-beacon.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/jsonld-fix.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/boot/breadcrumb-schema.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/site-settings.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/nav-dropdowns.js"}}"></script>
    {{!-- admin-auth.js (window.MOAuth.fetch) and the safe-href pair
         (window.MOSafeHref / window.MOSafeRedirect) are loaded earlier,
         right after the boot scripts and BEFORE {{{body}}} — see the
         comment at the top of <body> for why. Don't move them back
         down here without also wrapping every page-template hydration
         script in a "wait for window.MOAuth" guard. --}}
    <script src="{{asset "js/inline-signup.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/kit-events.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/dark-mode.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/feature-gate.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/search.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/boot/header-behaviors.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/commonplace.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/liturgical-calendar.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/slide-in.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/topic-filter.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/podcast-feed.js"}}"></script>
    <script src="{{asset "js/title-cleanup.js"}}"></script>

    <script src="{{asset "js/boot/viewport-fix.js"}}"></script>
    {{ghost_foot}}
</body>
</html>
